From d389392f3ba60319005d4cb6ecc890df77fe4327 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Tromey <tom@tromey.com>
Date: Fri, 8 Mar 2019 15:51:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] Introduce run_on_main_thread

This introduces a way for a callback to be run on the main thread.

gdb/ChangeLog
2019-11-26  Tom Tromey  <tom@tromey.com>

	* run-on-main-thread.c: New file.
	* run-on-main-thread.h: New file.
	* unittests/main-thread-selftests.c: New file.
	* Makefile.in (SUBDIR_UNITTESTS_SRCS): Add
	main-thread-selftests.c.
	(HFILES_NO_SRCDIR): Add run-on-main-thread.h.
	(COMMON_SFILES): Add run-on-main-thread.c.

Change-Id: I16ef82f0564e9f8a524bdc64cb31df79a988ad9f
---
 gdb/Makefile.in          |  2 +
 gdb/run-on-main-thread.c | 97 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 gdb/run-on-main-thread.h | 28 ++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 127 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 gdb/run-on-main-thread.c
 create mode 100644 gdb/run-on-main-thread.h

diff --git a/gdb/Makefile.in b/gdb/Makefile.in
index 5614cc3386c..a7942e6c37f 100644
--- a/gdb/Makefile.in
+++ b/gdb/Makefile.in
@@ -1100,6 +1100,7 @@ COMMON_SFILES = \
